    "created_at": "2021-01-27T19:05:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-01-27T19:48:52Z",
    "body": "I have also encountered issues with Debian. In my case, it is `gnome-terminal`. However, this may still be useful.\r\n\r\nI tried any number of things that I thought _should_ make my nerdfonts work, verified they were available, configured in in gnome settings, being used otherwise by gnome-terminal...\r\n\r\nJust this afternoon, I installed `fonts-symbola` (`apt install fonts-symbola`), and magically emojis in the starship prompt began to work. I confirmed that removal of that package subsequently broke them, and re-installation restored them.\r\n\r\nFurther testing found that `apt install fonts-noto-color-emoji` also has the same effect. I had another machine where emojis _where_ working without `fonts-symbola` installed, and found that `fonts-noto-color-emoji` was installed instead, and emojis could likewise be broken/repaired by removing/installing that package.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
